WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.340
Marvel's Black Widow' fills in Natasha Romanoff's
backstory — and along the way, it sets up

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:10.010
plenty of juicy possibilities for the future
of the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:14.610
The post-credits sequence in particular ties
together the stories of Black Widow, Avengers:

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:19.340
Endgame, The Falcon and the Winter Soldier,
and even the upcoming Hawkeye series, paving

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:23.710
the way for a seriously involved small-screen
situation within the MCU.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:29.010
Black Widow is set after the events of 2016's
Captain America: Civil War and prior to those

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:33.710
of 2018's Avengers: Infinity War, but the
film's post-credits scene takes viewers to

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:37.440
an entirely different section of the MCU’s
timeline.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.230
After the credits roll, the extra scene of
the new film jumps forward in time to the

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:47.060
world after Avengers: Endgame, focusing on
Nat's sister figure Yelena Belova in Ohio.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:51.760
She's mourning Nat, who gave her life to secure
the Soul Stone on Vormir during the time heist

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:52.890
event in Endgame.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:56.760
While Yelena is standing in front of Nat's
grave, a woman approaches her.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.360
You recognize her, right?

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:04.199
“Valentina Allegra de la Fontaine, actually
it’s the Contessa Valentina Allegra de la

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:05.199
Fontaine”

00:01:05.199 --> 00:01:06.840
You may also know her as Madame Hydra.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.891
Additionally, you know her as the woman who
recruited John Walker to her cause in The

00:01:10.891 --> 00:01:12.470
Falcon and the Winter Soldier.

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:17.560
“It’s hard, but I don’t like to repeat
myself so you can just call me Val, but don’t

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:19.799
call me Val, just keep it in your head.”

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:25.170
Valentina is looking to set Yelena on an ill-advised
revenge tour, which could shake the MCU.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:30.070
Variety confirmed back in December 2020 that
Florence Pugh is set to reprise her role in

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:35.909
the upcoming Hawkeye TV show, starring Jeremy
Renner as Clint Barton and MCU newcomer Hailee

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:38.250
Steinfeld as Kate Bishop, Clint's protégé.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:43.140
Based on what Val says to Yelena in the post-credits
sequence of "Black Widow," it seems likely

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:45.780
that she won't be showing up to help our heroes.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:49.920
After Yelena chides Val for interrupting her
during her vacation, Val gets straight to

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:50.920
the point.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:55.330
Before handing Yelena a tablet showing a photo
of Clint Barton, the Contessa says,

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:58.549
"Maybe you'd like a shot at the man responsible
for your sister's death.

00:01:58.549 --> 00:02:00.540
Kind of a cutie, don't you think?"

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:04.659
It's certainly a bit of a stretch to call
Clint "responsible" for Natasha's death — they

00:02:04.659 --> 00:02:08.869
both did everything they could to sacrifice
themselves on that mountain top — but The

00:02:08.869 --> 00:02:11.510
Contessa isn't known for being a straight-shooter.

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:15.920
We can infer from this interaction that Yelena
has come to work for the Contessa, much like

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.710
John Walker did at the end of "The Falcon
and the Winter Soldier."

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:23.510
It seems Madame Hydra is amassing a team of
killers much like General Dreykov's Black

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.510
Widows.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:28.890
A new power player is already taking his place
in the MCU espionage world, and she might

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.400
even have something to do with the Secret
Invasion.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:36.810
Julia Louis-Dreyfus' appearance in the "Black
Widow" post-credits scene was definitely unexpected,

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:40.140
but it wasn't quite as surprising as it was
originally supposed to be.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:45.590
Before the COVID-19 pandemic hit in early
2020, Louis-Dreyfus was set to join the MCU

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:50.730
during the post-credits scene of Black Widow,
but we all know what happened in 2020, so…

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:53.400
goodbye original MCU plans!

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.700
After re-shuffling the order a bit, Valentina
made her debut on The Falcon and the Winter

00:02:57.700 --> 00:02:58.700
Soldier.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:02.140
You can watch Julia Louis-Dreyfus in both
Black Widow and The Falcon and the Winter

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:07.660
Soldier on Disney+ — it’s an extra $29.99
for the movie, the series is no additional

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:10.019
charge to your monthly subscription.

